+	// allocation used to live here, guarded by "if (m_n_planes == 0)" /
+	// "if (m_image_memory == nullptr)" so a cold boot (the only caller
+	// this device used to have) did it exactly once. device_start() now
+	// does both unconditionally and earlier, so the buffer is already
+	// allocated and sized by the time device_reset() runs on every cold
+	// boot AND on a hardware reset — the two guards above would never
+	// fire again, so the dead branches are gone rather than left as
+	// unreachable code. device_reset() still needs to run on every actual
+	// reset to blank the screen and colour table (a LOADST restore does
+	// NOT call device_reset(), so this has no effect on the checkpoint
+	// path — it only re-zeroes an active boot/reset).
 	memset(m_color_lookup_table, 0, sizeof(m_color_lookup_table));
 	memset(m_image_memory.get(), 0, m_image_memory_size * 2);
 
